1 NOTE 1944 Dec Quarter death registration-
2 CONT Name: Hockley, Peter D---Age: 20
2 CONT District: Selby (Vol &amp;amp; Page: 9c 872)
2 CONT 
2 CONT In the early afternoon of 18 Nov 1944, Handley Page Halifax B.Mk III MZ559 aircraft of 578 RAF Squadron took flight from RAF Burn for a bombing operation over Munster, Germany. Returning after this operation, the Halifax was making a landing approa
2 CONC ch when, tragically, it collided in mid-air with another Halifax [Halifax NR241 from 51 RAF Squadron]. Both aircraft crash-landed, taking the lives of fourteen young airmen--all the aircrew of both aircraft.
2 CONT The seven airmen of Handley Page Halifax B.Mk III Halifax MZ559 who perished in this accident were--
2 CONT RAFVR Flight Sergeant Peter Wyper RATTRAY,
2 CONT RAFVR Flying Officer Thomas Ieuan Milner EVANS,
2 CONT RAFVR Sergeant John Charles CORDERY,
2 CONT RAFVR Flight Sergeant Clifford SAVERY,
2 CONT RAFVR Flying Officer William Henry BUSH,
2 CONT RAFVR Pilot Officer Kenneth Robert ARMSTRONG and
2 CONT RAF Pilot Officer Joseph Harold CHESTER.
2 CONT The seven airmen of Halifax NR241 who perished in this accident were--
2 CONT RAFVR Pilot Officer John William BRUCE,
2 CONT RAFVR Sergeant Jack BIDWELL,
2 CONT RAAF Flight Sergeant Cyril COLLAS,
2 CONT RAFVR Flight Sergeant John Dennis SUFFOLK,
2 CONT RAFVR Sergeant Peter Desmond HOCKLEY,
2 CONT RAFVR Sergeant Thomas Leslie SUMNER and
2 CONT RAFVR Sergeant John Charles Wilfred SMITH.
2 CONT 
2 CONT Military Service:-
2 CONT Rank: Sergeant
2 CONT Trade: Wireless Operator/Air Gunner
2 CONT Service Number: 1623536
2 CONT Age: 20
2 CONT Service: Royal Air Force Volunteer Reserve
2 CONT Division: 51 RAF Squadron
2 CONT Flowers
2 CONT 
2 CONT Plant Memorial Trees
2 CONT 
2 CONT Remembering Sergeant Peter Desmond HOCKLEY, with gratitude.
2 CONT 
2 CONT Left by SJB Hearn on 21 Jun 2018
