1 NOTE 1798 Thomas was born  to Robert Watts and Elizabeth,  December 1798, in Bethnal Green, London.
2 CONT 
2 CONT 1825 In October 1825 he married Elizabeth Sarah Evans in St Brides Church, Fleet Street, London
2 CONT 
2 CONT 1841 The 1841 census describes Thomas as a Brickmaker - as were most of his immediate neighbours. His children with Elizabeth are listed as follows
2 CONT 
2 CONT Mary 15
2 CONT Robert 14
2 CONT Thomas 11
2 CONT Samuel 9
2 CONT Elizabeth 7
2 CONT Hallen 5
2 CONT John 4
2 CONT Richard 2
2 CONT 
2 CONT They were to have 3 more children together before Thomas's death in 1845 - Charles, James and Lydia.
2 CONT 
2 CONT 1845 Thomas died in February 1845 in Bexley, Erith, Kent. His death certificate says he died suddenly from internal causes. He was only 46 years old. The informant was the Coroner for Kent, a solicitor, Charles Joseph Carttar, from Greenwich.
