1 NOTE John Hockley wrote of his mother that she was a good housewife, that she baked her own bread and short cakes and plain food, made her childrens clothes and was a good nurse among the poor people in Wickford and Nevendon. The villagers called on he
2 CONC r when friends and relatives were sick or dying. She even helped "to lay them out in their coffins".
