1 NOTE As a child Hilda lived with her parents and 5 brothers &amp; 4 sisters at 1 Northend Cottages - a group of 4/6 railway cottages close to the railway line between Jumbo Bridge and Tilbury Dock Station. In order to get to the shops, school, church o
2 CONC r anywhere else it was necessary to walk up the railway line and across a field before reaching habitation. As with the rest of the family Hilda attended St Mary's Church  and the  Church of England school at Little Thurrock.  Hilda worked as a nur
2 CONC sing auxiliary at Orsett Hospital until she married Charlie Pinnock, a personnel clerk at Thames Board Mills, in 1936.  Her interests were mainly round the home and family and the church where she used to sing in the choir. She was also a good gard
2 CONC ener and spent a lot of time growing vegetables and flowers. She was married some time before having children and she had several misccarriages before the birth of her first son, Stephen in 1943. Interested in music, she played the piano all her li
2 CONC fe.  Hilda was left a widow in 1977, contracted cancer and died in April 1982 at the age of 68. Before she died she knitted a matinee jacket for her great-great nephew Benjamin Hockley who was born the month following her death on 10th May.
