1 NOTE 
2 CONT 1810 George was born Abt. 1810 and baptised on 14/10/1810.
2 CONT 
2 CONT 1839 He married Eliza Rutland on 20/5/1839. The marriage was part of a double wedding ceremony with his sister, Catherine Coleman and William Hoare. His profession on the wedding certificate is recorded as 'Waterman'. A Waterman is defined by Wikip
2 CONC edia as "a river worker who transfers passengers across and along city centre rivers and estuaries in the United Kingdom". Bagshaw’s History, Gazetteer and Directory of Kent 1847 records that "The river Swale is crossed by Elmley Ferry" and it is t
2 CONC herefore likely that George was the Ferryman at the time of his marriage.
2 CONT 
2 CONT 1841 In the census of 1841 George's profession is recorded as Licenced Victualler at Elmley Ferry House and has therefore taken over the running of the Inn from his father, James Coleman, Bagshaw’s History, Gazetteer and Directory of Kent in 1847 h
2 CONC ad the following entry - "George Coleman, Vict. Elmley Ferry House Inn."
2 CONT 
2 CONT 1849 George died from a head injury on the 19/2/1849, aged just 39, leaving the running of the Inn to his wife Eiza. The death was attended by a Henry Rutland from Sittingbourne.
