1 NOTE Little is known about Phillip Scott. I have conjectured that the circumstantial evidence may be in favour of a Philip Scott residing in St Pancras (1901 census) with a McCarthy family originally from Co. Tipperary on the grounds that one John McCar
2 CONC thy was living at Crown Hall farm, Mucking, Essex in the Spooner household. It is thought he died in 1911 in Manchester. There is no evidence of his marriage to Mabel Spooner or of his death. He does however appear on my fathers Birth certificate.I
2 CONC t is thought he may have travelled to India and bought rolls of silk to resell in Manchester. PS There is another relevant Philip Scott a mill worker who lived in Haslingden but I have been unable to trace his whereabouts after 1901, except for ref
2 CONC erence as a crew member on the SS Iberia sailing from Liverpool to New york in 1911.He was employed as a groom for a Newmarket stable. Possibly the Tipperary Phillip Scott emigrated to USA in Sept 1910 on SS Minneapolis from Tilbury to NewYork
