1 NOTE As a child Cecil lived with his parents and 4 brothers &amp; 5 sisters at 1 Northend Cottages - a group of 4/6 railway cottages close to the railway line between Jumbo Bridge and Tilbury Dock Station. In order to get to the shops, school, church o
2 CONC r anywhere else it was necessary to walk up the railway line and across a field before reaching habitation. As with the rest of the family Cecil attended St Mary's Church  and the  Church of England school at Little Thurrock.
2 CONT 
2 CONT Cecil, a crane driver at Thomas Ward in Grays, was a happy go lucky sort of chap who learned to play the piano by ear and was the life and soul of many a family party. He really enjoyed life as a young man, went on outings to Ostend at weekends an
2 CONC d was very good to his mother.
2 CONT 
2 CONT He made a disastrous marriage to Mabel and eventually divorced her. He subsequently remarried and is believed to have found happiness.
