1 NOTE As a child Alf lived with his parents and 4 brothers &amp; 5 sisters at 1 Northend Cottages - a group of 4/6 railway cottages close to the railway line between Jumbo Bridge and Tilbury Dock Station. In order to get to the shops, school, church or a
2 CONC nywhere else it was necessary to walk up the railway line and across a field before reaching habitation. As with the rest of the family Alf attended St Mary's Church  and the  Church of England school at Little Thurrock.  He was killed in the 1914-
2 CONC 18 War and his name appears on the cenotaph at the junction of Rectory Road and Chadwell Road near Grays, Essex  and the war memorial at St Mary's, Ilford, Essex.
