1 NOTE As a child Chris lived with his parents and 4 brothers &amp; 5 sisters at 1 Northend Cottages - a group of 4/6 railway cottages close to the railway line between Jumbo Bridge and Tilbury Dock Station. In order to get to the shops, school, church o
2 CONC r anywhere else it was necessary to walk up the railway line and across a field before reaching habitation. As with the rest of the family Chris attended St Mary's Church and the Church of England school at Little Thurrock
2 CONT 
2 CONT Chris served in the Army of the Rhine following the first World War. He subsequently worked as a shunter for the PLA retiring as a foreman.
2 CONT 
2 CONT He divorced his first wife Meg while his daughters were in their teens and remarried. His second wife was one of the first people to have a heart valve replacement.
