1 NOTE Samuel's brother, John, records that Samuel had been a wicked young man and "left home through his wickedness". John does not make clear exactly where he went  but describes it as "many miles down in the country away from us all". Whilst working o
2 CONC n a high building Samuel fell on his head and almost broke his neck. He was hospitalised and it was a considerable time before word reached his mother of his whereabouts. She looked after him and brought him back home.
