1 NOTE Ellen Jane (aka Ginny) was a very small lady (5 feet tall or less) with one leg shorter than the other. A kindly soul much put upon by her husband and youngest son (Walter). She, like her husband, enjoyed the garden and grew flowers, particualarl
2 CONC y roses and soft fruits. She made jams, chutneys, pickles and fruit wines and kept a comfortable home for all the family. She suffered early senile dementia and died in a hospital for the mentally disturbed at Warley in Essex.
