1 NOTE As a child Lily lived with her parents and 5 brothers &amp; 4 sisters at 1 Northend Cottages - a group of 4/6 railway cottages close to the railway line between Jumbo Bridge and Tilbury Dock Station. In order to get to the shops, school, church o
2 CONC r anywhere else it was necessary to walk up the railway line and across a field before reaching habitation. As with the rest of the family lily attended St Mary's Church and the Church of England school at Little Thurrock.  She learned to play th
2 CONC e piano, moved to London to work in a hospital and was then married  to jim Hill, a policeman, in 1940. They were the most comfortable of all the family even owning a car in the year they were married.  Lilly and her children evacuated to Hexham, D
2 CONC urham during the Second World War while Jim remained in London during the blitz.
