1 NOTE Charlie worked as a signalman for 50 years with the London Midland &amp; Scottish Railway mostly stationed at Grays West.  Over 6 feet tall, he was a strict disciplinarian and churchgoer, a midwife once referring to him as "an outside angel and a
2 CONC n indoor devil". Neverthless, the family recognised him as a good father in that he ensured that they were well fed and took an interest in them and their activities.  A great gardener, he won many prizes for his vegetables at different shows and m
2 CONC ade gallons of different sorts of wine which all the family appreciated.  He always rode a bicycle and right up until he was aged over 65 he would ride every Wednesday to the Dog and Partridge public house (knwn locally as the Lime Kilns) which wa
2 CONC s situated about 5 miles from his home in Bulphan.  He died of a heart attack whilst using his daughter's lavatory.
