1 NOTE Len worked as a bricklayer until he contracted tubercolosis but then did not work at all for 25 years. At some stage he also had smallpox.  He married an Amy Martin who was Secretary to the West Thurrock Women's Guild and despite a shortage of mone
2 CONC y they lived comfortably together.  With the onset of the NHS he was sent for a medical examionation at Southend Hospital where it was found that his lungs had completely healed He was told he had to take a light job and became a nightwatchma
2 CONC n - a position he held until he retired..  He died of a heart attack whilst eating an orange.
