1 NOTE Percy worked at the Lafarge Aluminous Cement Works all his working life. He was a good worker, thought highly of and finished as a foreman.  A rather shy man he remained unmarried and for most of his life lived at home with his Mother. As a young m
2 CONC an he played football for a local team.  There was never any particular woman in his life other than his mother whom he cared for when she became bedridden. He was at her bedside when she died.  In later life he became ill himself and he moved in w
2 CONC ith his older brother Ben and his wife, Emily (Dot) who cared for him.
