1 NOTE Sidney worked all his working life at Thames Board Mills until he was killed there by a bomb blast in about 1942.  He was the only fatal casualty at Thames Board Mills during the 2nd World War. When the siren sounded he forgot his lunch sandwiche
2 CONC s before making his way to the shelter inside the factory. The bomb hit the entrance of the shelter whilst Sidney was returning to his place of work to collect the sandwiches.  He married an Ethel Pratt, a fat lazy woman, not much liked by the res
2 CONC t of the family.
2 CONT 
