1 NOTE [[During the war Anita moved with her mother to Buxton in Derbyshire where she received her early education at the local convent school.
2 CONT 
2 CONT After the war she returned to Essex with her mother and pusued a career in the Civil Service as a Clerical Officer. In 1958 she met and married Brian Ham whilst working at the North Thames Gas Board in Grays,  and subsequently moved with Brian to I
2 CONC pswich in Suffolk.
2 CONT 
2 CONT Anita was able to do anything she set her mind to. As well as being an avid reader and very knowledgeable she had many interests including needlework and, like her mother, was an excellent seamstress making many of her own clothes.
2 CONT 
2 CONT With her husband Brian, Anita was a great support to her two sons particularly during their years at university.]]
