1 _META <metadataxml><content><line>&lt;p&gt;From:&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;www.lib.byui/exhibits/Presidents/cole&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;quot;Julia was born in Clarkston, Utah.&amp;nbsp; She was a gentle person with a kindly sense of humor.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&am
2 CONC p;quot;There were many hardships in starting the Church in Northern California.&amp;nbsp; Julia was the first LDS woman in the area, and became a real pioneer, along with George, for good will, peace, missionary work and more.&amp;nbsp; Her famil
2 CONC y tells about the time when Julia was asked if Mormons had horns.&amp;nbsp; She told them, &amp;quot;Yes, we have horns.&amp;nbsp; Wait just a moment and I&amp;#39;ll go and get them.&amp;quot;&amp;nbsp; She went into the study and returned with mu
2 CONC sical instruments!&amp;nbsp; Having a sense of humor and a love of music also helped Julia and George deal with opposition when times were tough in settling the Church in Northern California.&amp;nbsp; Having faith in God strengthened their work fu
2 CONC rther.&amp;quot;&lt;/p&gt;</line></content></metadataxml>
