1 DATE 19th &amp; 25th Feb. 1999
1 _DSCR Echoes from the Past
1 _META <metadataxml><content><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;font face="arial,helvetica,sans-serif"&gt;&lt;font size="2"&gt;Elizabeth lost her mother when she was 4 years old. Following her father&amp;#39;s remarriage to&amp;nbsp; Reasha, Elizabeth went to live with h
2 CONC er step-mother at Pittown. She went to school at the Wallsend Public School leaving early to&amp;nbsp; take up domestic work.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;During the influenza epidemic the Wallsend School was turned int
2 CONC o a make-shift hospital, Elizabeth helped out there for some time.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Elizabeth met Alfred Lisle Ellevsen and after a courtship they married at the home of Mrs. Camps (a church member) at Waratah St, Newtown. Elder Robert Taylor fro
2 CONC m the Saints Church performed the ceremony. Witnesses to the marriage were Charles Royston Camps and Nelllie Camps. 9 children were born to this union. The family had a very close relationship with the Saints Church both at West Wallsend and Wallse
2 CONC nd. Later in life Elizabeth became Secretary to the women&amp;#39;s department.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Elizabeth passed away at the age of 52yrs in the Wallsend Hospital from kidney failure. Services were from the Saints Church, Wallsend and the gravesi
2 CONC de at Wallsend Cemetery. &lt;/p&gt;</line></content></metadataxml>
