2 TITL Houses in Rectory Road
1 _OID d135f14e-5971-44fe-89a1-b21eeeb134b0
1 _META <metadataxml><content><line>&lt;span&gt;&lt;font size="3"&gt;&lt;font face="Times New Roman"&gt;Dad said that William Johnson Jennings worked for Walsham&amp;rsquo;s the builders (who also built 68 Bradleigh Avenue).&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span
2 CONC &gt;He bought a 2-bedroomed Walsham house in Rosedale Avenue.&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;He later bought another 4, and the family moved into the new ones as they were bought, renting the old ones out each time.&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/s
2 CONC pan&gt;Then, about 1912, they moved to 123 Rectory Road.&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;Dad therefore reckons that 123 Rectory Road is &amp;ldquo;Ivanhoe&amp;rdquo;, where James Beard lived with daughter Nellie at the time of his death (accordi
2 CONC ng to his death certificate). About 1937, when Walsham built 100 Rectory Road (the bungalow), the Jennings family moved there, primarily because Nellie supposedly had a bad heart (she lived for another 39 years&amp;hellip;..).&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp
2 CONC ; &lt;/span&gt;The houses in Rosedale Avenue were sold for a total of &amp;pound;1,250 in the 1970s.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/span&gt;</line></content></metadataxml>
