1 _OID d5ab14a7-8564-4953-9095-445b8f95ea71
1 _META <metadataxml><content><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: times; font-size: small; line-height: normal; text-align: -webkit-;"&gt;George Cole was born and reared in American Fork, Utah. He was the youngest of five children. His parents join
2 CONC ed the Church in England, came to America in 1853 and settled in American Fork.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br style="font-family: times; font-size: small; line-height: normal; text-align: -webkit-;"&gt;&lt;br style="font-family: times; font-size: small; line-
2 CONC height: normal; text-align: -webkit-;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: times; font-size: small; line-height: normal; text-align: -webkit-;"&gt;He married Rosalie Jane Henault in 1890 in Logan, Utah. He taught school in Malad, Idaho for several year
2 CONC s. He was called to be principal of Bannock Academy in 1894, when Charles Watkins resigned as principal of the Academy for health reasons. Seventh and eighth grade school work was introduced at the Academy while George was principal.&lt;/span&gt;&l
2 CONC t;br style="font-family: times; font-size: small; line-height: normal; text-align: -webkit-;"&gt;&lt;br style="font-family: times; font-size: small; line-height: normal; text-align: -webkit-;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: times; font-size: small
2 CONC ; line-height: normal; text-align: -webkit-;"&gt;The Academy struggled to stay open. The economic situation was such that George Cole and the other four teachers taught the last half of one year without pay. They accepted homegrown produce instea
2 CONC d of cash for students' tuitions. This way their families had food to eat.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br style="font-family: times; font-size: small; line-height: normal; text-align: -webkit-;"&gt;&lt;br style="font-family: times; font-size: small; line-heigh
2 CONC t: normal; text-align: -webkit-;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: times; font-size: small; line-height: normal; text-align: -webkit-;"&gt;George's wife, Rosalie, died in 1897 at the birth of their fourth child. He continued as principal and as a te
2 CONC acher until 1899 when he resigned. He married Mary Julia Goodey in 1900 in Salt Lake City, but they continued to live in Rexburg. In 1906, George and Julia Cole were sent by the Church to colonize the first permanent Mormon settlement in Northern C
2 CONC alifornia. They departed cold, windy Rexburg in the fall of that year with several other families and moved to sunny Gridley, located 70 miles north of Sacramento. George and Julia built a home in Gridley where the first meetings of the Church wer
2 CONC e held.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br style="font-family: times; font-size: small; line-height: normal; text-align: -webkit-;"&gt;&lt;br style="font-family: times; font-size: small; line-height: normal; text-align: -webkit-;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: t
2 CONC imes; font-size: small; line-height: normal; text-align: -webkit-;"&gt;Soon Gridley had more than fifty members of the Church and a branch was organized with George as the Branch President. He served in that capacity for several years.&lt;/span&gt;
2 CONC &lt;br style="font-family: times; font-size: small; line-height: normal; text-align: -webkit-;"&gt;&lt;br style="font-family: times; font-size: small; line-height: normal; text-align: -webkit-;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: times; font-size: sma
2 CONC ll; line-height: normal; text-align: -webkit-;"&gt;George was an able and talented musician and led the church choir for many years. He was active in his community. He served several years as the secretary of the Gridley Federal Farm Loan Associati
2 CONC on. George died in Gridley in 1932 and is buried there.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: times; font-size: small; line-height: normal; text-align: -webkit-;"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&
2 CONC lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: times; font-size: small; line-height: normal; text-align: -webkit-;"&gt;Source:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;http://www.lib.byui.edu/exhibits/Presidents/cole2.html&lt;/p&gt;</line></content></metadataxml>
