1 NOTE 
2 CONT "Barrie and I were told by our mother that her first- born was a son, Graham, who tragically died at the age of two, when she was pregnant with Barrie.  It would seem that gastric flu was rife at the time and Graham was given that diagnosis when i
2 CONC n fact he had appendicitis.  Because of the delay he developed septicaemia, and consequently died.  It seems our father was quite a well-known footballer, and it was reported in the local newspaper that a fellow team player had volunteered matche
2 CONC d blood for a transfusion, but it was too late to save Graham.  It must have been a dreadful time for our parents." Sue Hayes (Shorthose)
