1 NOTE "....I had acute Appendicitis when I was 10y 6m, and in my first year at Weymouth Grammar School.
2 CONT I became ill on an early Saturday morning in March 1946 and was put to bed. On Monday my grandparents called our Doctor (I wonder how they contacted him. There was a phone box across the street, about 100 yards away) and he arrived late morning. Hi
2 CONC s immediate reaction was to call an Ambulance and I was taken to Margaret Mitchell Men’s Ward in Weymouth &amp; District Hospital. An hour later I was “under the knife. In those days, an Appendectomy meant 2 weeks in hospital." (John Dukes)
